@* The spinelly. wordmark, inlined rather than referenced with <img src>.

   Both source files paint with currentColor, and an <img> renders an SVG as an isolated
   document: currentColor would resolve against that document's own default, which is
   black, and the mark would disappear into the footer. Inlining lets it inherit colour
   from the page, so one CSS rule tints it and the hover state works.

   The trailing dot keeps its own accent (--brand-accent, falling back to spinelly's
   lilac) rather than being tinted with the rest — it is the distinguishing part of the
   mark and belongs to that brand, not this one.

   aria-hidden because the anchor around it carries the label; without that a screen
   reader announces the destination twice. *@

